# Copy to core/.env and fill in. core/.env is gitignored; never commit it, and
# never read it into anything under src/ — the browser must not see a key.
#
# Set a spend limit in the Anthropic console before the first call. Not because
# the volume is risky, but because a cap turns a runaway loop from a bill into
# a bug report.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# PostgreSQL, the one store (ADR-001). `pnpm db:up` starts the developer's
# database (compose.yaml) at this address and `pnpm db:migrate` brings it to the
# newest schema. On the always-on host the database is named `openferment`,
# which `pnpm db:reset` refuses to drop.
OPENFERMENT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://openferment:openferment@127.0.0.1:5432/openferment_dev
# The tests make a database of their own for each run on this server, named
# after this address's database (core/tests/conftest.py). This is the default.
# OPENFERMENT_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://openferment:openferment@127.0.0.1:5432/openferment_test

# Optional. Which models answer, and how hard they think (core/openferment_core/llm.py).
# Defaults: Claude Opus 5.5 first, Claude Sonnet 5.5 when Opus declines or is
# unavailable, effort medium (low, medium, high, xhigh or max). Leave them
# commented out to use the defaults. OPENFERMENT_FALLBACK_MODEL may name several
# models, comma-separated, tried in order after the first.
# OPENFERMENT_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# OPENFERMENT_FALLBACK_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# OPENFERMENT_EFFORT=medium

# Optional. The model for bulk index chores (OF-BLD-014 E.7): retrieval helper
# calls and writing evaluation questions. Falls back to the chain above.
# OPENFERMENT_INDEX_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# Optional. The routing table (core/openferment_core/llm.py, ROUTES), laid over
# the models above family by family: plan (Postdoc's loop), explain (an answer
# in one call), extract, index and judge, each {"models": [...], "effort": ...}.
# A model is provider:model in Sci RAG Kit's syntax, a bare id Anthropic's; the
# service serves Anthropic's models, and a route naming another provider waits
# for the owner's decision on how its key is read. `pnpm ready` checks it.
# OPENFERMENT_ROUTES={"judge": {"models": ["anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5"], "effort": "low"}}

# Optional. Spend guards inside the service (OF-BLD-014 D8), in US dollars.
# The daily cap covers every model call in a UTC day; llm.py refuses a call
# that could pass it. The per-question cap bounds one Postdoc question (§5.2).
# OPENFERMENT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=25

# A key that is not scoped to a workspace is accepted only with the workspace
# named on each request (the API answers 400 and says so). Put the workspace's
# id here; it is sent as the anthropic-workspace-id header. Not a secret.
# OPENFERMENT_WORKSPACE_ID=
# OPENFERMENT_ASK_BUDGET_USD=0.75
